       "number": 753,
       "title": "Subclassed decorator methods not working",
       "body": "My framework relies on (smart) subclassing, but I've also got it to work with attrs mostly. Running into a problem like the following.\r\n\r\n```\r\n@attr.s\r\nclass BaseClass():\r\n    \r\n    value = attr.ib(default=10)\r\n\r\n@attr.s\r\nclass TestClass(BaseClass):\r\n    \r\n    @value.default\r\n    def _not_value(self):\r\n        return 20\r\n```",
